{"name":"Sanderling","hex":"#c8ab96","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sanderling","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small wading bird, of species Calidris alba, that breeds in the Arctic and winters on sandy shores and estuaries around the world."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sanderling"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sanderling","blocks":[{"text":"The sanderling is a small wading bird. It is a circumpolar Arctic breeder, being among the most extreme northern breeding birds in the world, nesting only on the coldest tundra, north of the 5°C July isotherm; in Europe, its southernmost breeding locality is Svalbard, where only a handful (5–15) pairs breed. It is a long-distance migrant, wintering south to South America, western and southern Europe, Africa, and Australia. It is highly gregarious in winter, sometimes forming large flocks on coastal mudflats or sandy beaches."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Sanderling_%28Calidris_alba%29_in_Breeding_Plumage_in_the_Delaware_Bay_-_Heislerville_WMA_-_Cumberland_County_-_New_Jersey_-_May_2026.jpg/330px-Sanderling_%28Calidris_alba%29_in_Breeding_Plumage_in_the_Delaware_Bay_-_Heislerville_WMA_-_Cumberland_County_-_New_Jersey_-_May_2026.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanderling"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Sanderling_%28Calidris_alba%29_starting_to_get_breeding_plumage%2C_Heislerville_WMA%2C_New_Jersey%2C_USA.png/500px-Sanderling_%28Calidris_alba%29_starting_to_get_breeding_plumage%2C_Heislerville_WMA%2C_New_Jersey%2C_USA.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Sanderling_%28Calidris_alba%29_starting_to_get_breeding_plumage%2C_Heislerville_WMA%2C_New_Jersey%2C_USA.png/1280px-Sanderling_%28Calidris_alba%29_starting_to_get_b